WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.030
Kia ora kotou

00:00:02.030 --> 00:00:05.700
Warm greetings to everyone in our community.

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:10.530
Firstly, I want to acknowledge that for many
of you it’s been a difficult week.

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:17.700
I know there’s a high level of uncertainty
and things are changing almost on a daily basis.

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:23.960
I need to reassure you that the Council is
working extremely hard to support our community

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:31.100
and ensure all our essential services - water, roading, recycling and rubbish

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:35.060
will continue to operate smoothly through this difficult time.

00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:40.640
We have followed Ministry of Health guidelines
and shut all Council building and facilities

00:00:40.649 --> 00:00:43.710
in order protect our residents.

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:49.740
We are closely following the situation, and
as soon as it’s possible to reopen facilities,

00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:51.600
we will do so.

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:56.280
In the meantime we’re adapting and finding ways for people

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:59.579
to access council services remotely.

00:00:59.579 --> 00:01:04.930
Staff from departments such as the aquatic
facilities, are being redeployed to assist

00:01:04.930 --> 00:01:09.600
our community in other areas when it’s safe
to do so.

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:16.280
Our libraries already offer a great range
of digital services you can access from home.

00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:24.320
You can contact our Customer Services by email,
phone, Facebook or Snap, Send Solve.

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:30.400
As much as possible, we will still be carrying
out our normal activities, such as dog registrations,

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:32.780
LIMS and animal management.

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:38.880
We have streamlined our decision-making and
have formed a Covid 19 Response Committee

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:45.720
made up of Councillors, so our Council can
adapt quickly to any challenges that may arise.

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:50.380
Our Councillors are at this moment taking
another look through our budgets and at the

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:54.020
projects we had planned for the coming year.

00:01:54.020 --> 00:02:01.010
It’s important that our infrastructure is
maintained, that we support our local contractors

00:02:01.010 --> 00:02:03.880
and we keep planning for our future growth.

00:02:03.880 --> 00:02:10.619
However there may be spending that can be
deferred until this situation is behind us.

00:02:10.619 --> 00:02:16.280
I encourage you to listen and follow the advice
from the Government.

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:19.900
Remain calm, look after one another

00:02:19.900 --> 00:02:25.880
and when the restrictions ease, support our local businesses as much as you can.

00:02:25.890 --> 00:02:30.560
Our community is strong and resilient.

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:38.860
Our pandemic plans are up to date and Civil
Defence are ready to activate if needed.

00:02:38.860 --> 00:02:45.790
We have been through hard times before, and
together, united, we will beat this virus.

